    "['ethernet cfm mep [parameter1] domain [parameter2] service [parameter3] inward', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols oam ethernet connectivity-fault-management maintenance-domain md3 level 3', 'parent_command': ['set protocols oam ethernet connectivity-fault-management maintenance-domain md3 level 3 maintenance-association ma3 mep 3'], 'root': 'set protocols oam ethernet connectivity-fault-management maintenance-domain md3 level 3 maintenance-association ma3 mep 3', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the translated Juniper equivalent command for the Cisco CFM MEP inward configuration:\\n\\n##\\nset protocols oam ethernet connectivity-fault-management maintenance-domain md3 level 3\\nset protocols oam ethernet connectivity-fault-management maintenance-domain md3 maintenance-association ma3 mep 3 direction inward\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n1. The first command establishes the maintenance domain (MD) at level 3\\n2. The second command creates the MEP (Maintenance End Point) with ID 3 in the specified MA (Maintenance Association) and sets its direction to inward (equivalent to Cisco\\'s \"inward\" parameter)', 'trans_template': 'set protocols oam ethernet connectivity-fault-management maintenance-domain md3 level 3'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols oam ethernet connectivity-fault-management maintenance-domain md3 maintenance-association ma3 mep 3 direction inward', 'parent_command': ['set protocols oam ethernet connectivity-fault-management maintenance-domain md3 level 3 maintenance-association ma3 mep 3'], 'root': 'set protocols oam ethernet connectivity-fault-management maintenance-domain md3 level 3 maintenance-association ma3 mep 3', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the translated Juniper equivalent command for the Cisco CFM MEP inward configuration:\\n\\n##\\nset protocols oam ethernet connectivity-fault-management maintenance-domain md3 level 3\\nset protocols oam ethernet connectivity-fault-management main